+# Bug Addendum v001 — Zero-parent commit marshalling
+
+## Metadata
+
+- Bug: `BUG-20260817-T8MW`
+- Verdict: `spec-gap`
+- Addendum version: `v001`
+- Effective date: `2026-08-20`
+- Status: approved
+- Human decision: option 3 (`spec-gap`) selected in the Reversa fix workflow.
+
+## Target
+
+This addendum extends the History and Integration Operations requirements and
+edge cases. The original specifications remain unchanged.
+
+## Delta
+
+No prior normative requirement defines root commit creation or zero-parent FFI
+marshalling.
+
+## Normative Addition
+
+1. Commit creation APIs must support a root commit with zero parents.
+2. When `parentCount` is zero, the native parent pointer argument must be
+   `nullptr`, and no zero-element allocation may be indexed or dereferenced.
+3. When `parentCount` is greater than zero, the binding must allocate exactly
+   `parentCount` pointer elements and preserve the input parent order.
+4. The same invariant applies to commit creation, commit buffer creation, and
+   commit creation from object IDs.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+- A root commit can be created with an empty parent list.
+- A commit buffer can be created with an empty parent list and contains no
+  parent header.
+- A commit can be created from IDs with an empty parent list.
+- Source-level or allocator-instrumented verification confirms that the
+  zero-parent path does not write element zero of a zero-length pointer array.
+
